      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-guts-2003-p2.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "3\n\nThe equation \\(x^{4}-x^{2} y^{2}=0\\) factors as \\(x^{2}(x+y)(x-y)=0\\), so its graph is the union of the three lines \\(x=0, x+y=0\\), and \\(x-y=0\\).",
